WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience clapping)
- Alright.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.970
We always like to finish
up with something hopeful,

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:04.140
and today is no different.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.052
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.052 --> 00:00:07.800
(upbeat music)
(audience clapping)

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.920
Nearly 40 million people
here in the US have diabetes,

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.220
and the price of medication
and supplies can really add up.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.860
That's why one Arizona man
has made it his mission

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:20.640
to provide those necessities
to people in need for free,

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:21.720
which is incredible.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.240
And the world of TikTok
has been quick to help.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.820
Let's welcome the founder
of the Embrace Foundation,

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.530
watching on 3TV in Phoenix.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:29.891
What's up, Brandon?

00:00:29.891 --> 00:00:32.040
(audience cheering)

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:33.360
- Kelly, how you doing?

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.560
- [Kelly] I am so well.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.070
So, this was born out of
your own experience, right?

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.590
- Yeah, I was diagnosed
when I was seven years old

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:42.120
with Type 1 Diabetes.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.810
And in 2014, I aged outta
my parents' insurance,

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:48.570
so I was reusing pen needles,

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.630
I was skipping meals, skipping doses.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.910
I would actually go around
to different hospitals

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:57.600
and endocrinologist's, even
my pediatric endocrinologist,

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.520
which I saw when I was in middle school,

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.410
to beg for little sample sizes of insulin

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:04.620
just to kind of get me by
until I was able to secure

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.960
a full-time job with good
insurance and health benefits,

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.450
and things like that,
because it costs so much.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:11.550
It costs $700, if not more,

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:15.180
to sustain a diabetic lifestyle.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:18.180
And in America, it's the
only place that's like it,

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:21.300
every other country, they give
it away essentially for free.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.133
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:25.140
I can't imagine having
to beg for something,

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.760
obviously to live.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:27.600
That's incredible.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.570
So, can you tell us more
about the Embrace Foundation?

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.250
- Yeah, so, like I said,

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.170
there are so many other
Americans kind of going through

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:35.730
exactly what we're going through,

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:37.130
or what I was going through.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.740
Going to college, or maybe
they're a single parent

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.800
whose child was just
diagnosed with diabetes.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:46.170
So in 2020, I started
the Embrace Foundation,

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:49.020
and we are a nonprofit
organization that helps diabetics

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.360
all across the country get
the supplies that they need

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.833
for absolutely free.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:56.010
We started in 2020, and with TikTok,

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:58.380
we got a ton of support.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.750
We're getting supplies
from fellow diabetics

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.490
all over the country.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.290
We're getting monetary
donations from people.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.850
So, we're able to do it for free.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.373
And since our conception in 2020,

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.240
we are able to send
out over 4,000 supplies

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.178
to diabetics in need.

00:02:13.178 --> 00:02:14.878
(audience clapping)
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.450
So you're being the help
that you needed, man.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.100
That's incredibly cool, Brandon.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.307
I'm liking your post right now, alright?

00:02:22.307 --> 00:02:23.670
(bell rings)

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:24.810
- [Brandon] Okay, thank you.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:25.920
- And that's not all, my man.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.470
Our season long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of Frixion,

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:30.600
the go-to erasable pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show",

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.730
love how you're helping fellow patients,

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.170
and want to help you do more.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:35.790
So, they're gonna give
you a thousand dollars.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:36.623
How's that sound?

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:39.000
(audience cheering)
(audience clapping)

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:39.833
- Thank you so much.

00:02:39.833 --> 00:02:40.890
I appreciate it.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.930
I'm only listening to
Kelly Clarkson from now on.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:43.800
- Oh yeah!
- [Brandon] Only person I

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:44.633
thought about.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:46.950
- [Kelly] Thank you so much, Brandon.

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.618
Have a great 2023, alright.

00:02:48.618 --> 00:02:49.470
(audience cheering)
(audience clapping)

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:51.840
Alright, thank you to
all our guests this hour.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:54.837
Kate Walsh, Randy Jackson, Paul Rabil,

00:02:54.837 --> 00:02:56.100
Tim and Lauren Ziering.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:56.933
Y'all have a great day,

00:02:56.933 --> 00:02:59.010
and if it's not, well, try and change it.

